@dmweisberger @ltabb I’m not really demonizing it, but they used to market as the ppl who didn’t do it. No? https://t.co/1oZHrxFzRQ

Direct Indexing was a really solid attempt for asset managers to avoid having to brave the ETF Terrordome. I dont blame them for trying but to quote Michael Jordan “you still gotta come through Chicago”   And that’s we have been(bf it was cool) and will be bearish vs the hype

Tbf There are some specific cases for DI. Not saying it doesn’t exist but it was seen as legit competitor, even a replacement, to ETFs 10yrs ago. Tokenization is the new thing. So far I’m not impressed altho I definitely see tokenization distributing ETFs to people on chain.

@DaveNadig I’m not denying it exists but it underwhelmed vs hype. And I’m not sure about that flow number. How is that calc’d.  When I ask MS for parametric flows, they won’t tell me. But in the end the flows INTO ETFs tell the story anyway

